amon valani is obsessed with the comics  and specifically miss marvel's character  so getting cast as the hero was a dream  come true valani found out about the  casting call through her aunt who  forwarded her the information and valani  recalls it not looking too legit super  sketchy i don't know what casting calls  look like she sent in her audition tape  at 3 am and found out months later on  her last day of school that she had  landed the role this was actually her  first acting job which is an extremely  impressive way to kick off your career  number five can you imagine anyone else  playing the god of thunder in the mcu  apparently marvel initially could they  turned hemsworth down at first and chris  completely understood i think my  audition sucked i think that was that  was the response i got hemsworth had to  reach shakespearean s dialogue for his  audition  when i discovered an especially rare  breed of butterfly  so we can understand it being a little  difficult chris's younger brother liam  actually almost ended up landing the  role but was turned down for being too  young chris was then called back in and  he nailed it his second time around  number six how do you like them apples  simulu's first audition for shanghi  included reading two scenes from  goodwill hunting and liu couldn't resist  imitating matt damon i got my ten rings  ma it may seem like a weird choice but  casting director sarah finn was  impressed with everything he did he went  through a long and arduous audition  process and he completely nailed every  audition liu actually predicted his  casting way back when chongqi was first  announced he tweeted okay marvel we  gonna talk or what freaky  number seven doctor strange could have  looked very different director scott  derrickson had no doubts about who he  wanted to play the sorcerer supreme  benedict was always our first choice for  the role but even though cumberbatch had  an amazing audition and was offered the  role he initially couldn't take it due  to scheduling conflicts with another  project he was working on at the time  marvel wanted him so badly though that  they pushed back production of the movie  to accommodate cumberbatch that is some  real sorcery from benedict  number 8 we almost got a different black  widow emily blunt was actually cast  which really bummed out johansen i  wanted to work with john favreau and  robert downey jr and then i did not get  the role and i was pretty bummed about  that blonde had scheduling conflicts  which opened up the door for scarlett's  return and it's safe to say everyone was  happy about how things turned out we  knew that scarlet could bring the depth  and the texture to the character that we  wanted number nine tom is the true  trickster god so much so that he tried  auditioning for the role of thor in the  original movie the audition process  lasted three months and you already know  how it turned out for hiddleston what  you always wanted  he didn't land the role of thor but the  casting directors at marvel saw  something more mischievous in his future  the moment he came in and read though it  was loki number 10 it's ned's world and  we're just living in it jacob batalon  had very little acting experience before  his role as ned in spider-man homecoming  it was his first ever audition and he  never believed he would get the role  battalon said that the audition was  nerve-racking for him tom had a really  good time but i was shaking in my shoes  at least zendaya and tom holland both  seem to really enjoy batolon's audition  tapes number 11 chadwick boseman was a  true king through and through bozeman  originally auditioned to play drax in  guardians of the galaxy but he wasn't  quite the right fit for the character  the casting director said that bozeman  played the character like a king  every cell  in my body united in one single purpose  which didn't work for drax but did work  for another character they were  introducing two years later but when it  came time to cast black panther i was  very sure of him for that role  number 12 he is iron man robert downey  jr's audition went exactly how you would  expect it to go he had charisma charm  and had everyone in the room laughing  there it is there's a smile it's okay  yeah so it's natural less less muscles  to smile downey got into the mindset  that there was nobody else that could  possibly get the role but him i don't  want to caught an out about experience  but it was one of those rushes it seems  everyone in the world knows that hiring  downey as iron man was unquestionably  the right move i think hiring robert  downey jr was the best decision we've  ever made how about that  number 13 if it isn't star prince or  maybe it's captain america since that's  the role pratt initially auditioned for  and by the time you do jimmy could be  dead how do you know he isn't already  well i don't i'm not going to sit around  here and wait for someone to tell me he  didn't get that role and almost didn't  get the role of star ward as james gunn  resisted auditioning pratt and i went to  james and he said chris pratt  no way he's totally wrong gunn was  finally convinced to let pratt audition  and 10 seconds in james gunn looked at  casting director sarah finn and said  he's the guy pratt's screen test  alongside dave bautista featured some  hilarious improv and we can see why gunn  was so quick to change his mind it's a  cassette compilation tape  number 14 we stan stan the winter  soldier wanted to be captain america and  he gave a great audition he just wasn't  right for the part casting director  sarah finn said they saw a bit of  darkness in his performance that was  better suited for bucky  number 15 another actor who went for a  completely different role karen gillan  auditioned for agent 13 and captain  america the winter soldier but they saw  something else in her performance karen  was someone who was an incredibly  grounded and solid actor when they  brought her back in to read for nebula  they were originally going to let her  use her natural scottish accent which  you can hear in her audition tape the  disdain that brims only for our way of  life but i am at my brain james gunn  stated that gillen's audition was his  favorite of any of the guardians of the  galaxy actors  number 16 expect disappointment and  you'll never really be disappointed dave  bautista went into his audition for drax  with low expectations but that didn't  stop him from nailing his part he went  through months of auditioning and  chemistry tests which found him doing a  screen test alongside chris pratt he  bounced improv off him including his  famous finger on throat line why would i  put my finger on his throat it was an  instant connection between the two and  it was clear there was no other choice  for star-lord's right-hand man we didn't  know each other had never met each other  and we just clicked  number 17 roland's casting as thanos was  inevitable he wasn't sure how the motion  capture performance would work so he  watched videos of benedict cumberbatch  giving his mocap performance in the  hobbit he took inspiration from the  performance to create his own  performance as thanos he's such an  amazing performer and so uniquely suited  to thanos  number 18 higher further faster brie  larson first tried joining the marvel  empire back in phase 1 when she  auditioned for both thor and iron man 2.  years later marvel gave larson a call to  tell her they wanted her to play captain  marvel which she initially refused  multiple times oh i can't do that like i  have too much anxiety that's too much  for me um i don't think i can handle  that after several months she was  finally convinced to take the part after  reading the script and meeting all the  writers i remember my team being really  proud of me because they knew that it  was a big step for me number 19 from  disembodied voice to a real boy don't  forget paul bettany's vision was first  and foremost the ai voice of tony  stark's jarvis assistant betany had no  inkling of an idea back in 2008 that he  would ever get a chance to play the  vision in the mcu but when avengers age  of ultron came around joss whedon came a  knocking my phone rang and it was just  whedon and he said do you want to be the  vision in the avengers and i went yes i  do number 20. mackie's so good he never  even had to audition he was always  marvel's first choice to play the falcon  and they immediately offered him the  role we just offered him the role in my  memory he did not audition that's only  happened a handful of times at marvel  mackie did however audition for the  mandarin in iron man 3 which caught the  attention of winter soldier directors  the russo brothers he has charisma but  he also has the ability to convey  integrity in a way that very few actors  can we had no idea how different the  face of the mcu could have been if  things just went slightly different but  we're more than happy with what we got  and these actors proved that they  deserved the parts they landed which  audition story did you find most  surprising let us know down in the  comments and thanks for stopping by at  the things

